            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked whether a new guideline that reduces sentences by 10\u202fpercent would present any constitutional problems."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor questioned the constitutional difference that would give a Sixth Amendment right in resentencing versus a Bureau of Prisons modification."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia stated that the nature of the Sentencing Commission\u2019s policy statement, not the section itself, is unconstitutional."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked, \u201cWhat\u2019s unconstitutional about that?\u201d regarding the policy statement."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 33,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg inquired whether other guideline ranges have been reduced retroactively."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether the judge must consider a prisoner\u2019s behavior in prison when deciding a reduction under \u00a7\u202f3582(c)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0001-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts expressed concern that allowing judges to consider conduct in prison could open the door to many other factors."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether the Justice Department ever recommends commutations for prisoners like the respondent."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy noted that there were no commutations the prior year and five the year before."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether the statute would prohibit a more generous policy statement."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked for clarification on how the court can consider other factors under \u00a7\u202f3553 when making a reduction."
      }
    ],
