  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner argues that Sentencing Commission policy statements cannot override the Court\u2019s directive that sentencing guidelines are advisory."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner contends that imposing a mandatory guideline sentence that exceeds the jury\u2019s verdict violates the Sixth Amendment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Kruger",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 33,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Kruger, many guideline ranges have been reduced retroactively; the Sentencing Commission has made 27 retroactive amendments."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Kruger",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Kruger, the district court may consider any disciplinary proceedings that occurred during the defendant\u2019s imprisonment when deciding a sentence reduction."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Kruger",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0001-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Kruger, section\u202f3582(c)(2) directs that district courts have discretion to reduce sentences consistent with applicable policy statements, after considering the statutory factors in \u00a7\u202f3553(a)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Kruger",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0002-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The government takes these considerations into account when making recommendations about sentence reductions under \u00a7\u202f3582(c)(2)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Lisa B. Freeland",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c2bb2e1bd033ec407fad0c2c82571c36787e3ba6b0808b6819ac519ef187ee14",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c2bb2e1bd033-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Lisa B. Freeland, under rule\u202f1B1.10, courts are required (\u201cshall\u201d) to consider bad behavior in prison when deciding a sentence reduction."
      }
    ],
